From 7b03404bd7f0e08120af0836ce11a6b27d45f5b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thomas Klemm <github@tklemm.eu>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 09:56:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] ZJIT: Test sends with a Symbol block argument

Cover the cases where the interpreter does more than use the Symbol as
the block handler: Symbol#to_proc redefined before the send is compiled,
after it, with its own definition (also where the callee evicts the
Symbol Proc cache before it reads its block), and in another box;
another block argument object reaching the compiled send; refinements
in the caller, also ones that `using` adds after the send is compiled;
errors raised through the Symbol block; and a stack overflow exit that
re-executes the send.
